hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1386","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Yahya told us, Abdul Malik told us, Ata told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: It collapsed The sun was during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and that was the day his son Ibrahim, son of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, so he prayed. He led the people with six rak'ahs in four prostrations. He said \Allahu Akbar\"""," then he recited and prolonged the recitation"," then he bowed in the same way as he had stood"," then he raised his head and recited without The first reading"," then he bowed down as he recited"," then he raised his head"," so he read without the second reading"," then he kneeled down as he recited"," then raised his head. his head"," then he descended and prostrated two prostrations"," then he stood up and prayed three rak’ahs before he prostrated"," in which there was no rak’ah except the one before it that was longer than The one after that"," except that his bowing was like his standing"," then he delayed in his prayer and the rows delayed with him"," then he advanced and the rows advanced with him. He finished the prayer and the sun had shone"," then he said: “O people"," the sun and the moon are only two signs of God"," and they are not eclipsed by the death of a human being. So if you see any of that"," pray until you are saved.”"""
